[Music]  when I started I just you know I bought  20 sheets of plywood and just started  cutting I don't know how to build a boat  so it was a good design for me because  it was basically two shapes one is a  sphere one is a cylinder and just put  them together but tsunami ball is a 22  foot long a tanned 1/2 feet tall 10 feet  wide survival boat made of plywood and  epoxy he could put 1012 people in there  got the idea for working on the tsunami  ball I was I was in a startup incubator  in Silicon Valley and in one week we had  a presentation by an astronaut talking  about how asteroids might hit the planet  we should divert them or they caused  giant tsunamis and then two days later  that Japanese tsunami hit I spent a year  in Fukushima of course you imagined the  people that you know and the friends  that you had and you wonder if they're  okay it was a it was a hard thing the  idea is to design something that will be  comfortable on land so that if you lived  in a place that had tsunamis it would  just be in your backyard and when you'd  hear the alarm and the family would  climbed in and you'd be okay so it'll  sit in our backyard somewhere and it's  possible we'll try and do an Airbnb deal  where folks can come and check it out  and spend the night  I don't know what I've spent so far I  kind of look at it as I'm taking my  retirement early while I have the  ability to jump up and down and lift  heavy objects I've been at some fairly  successful startups which is also helped  with the budget for the boat the biggest  one was PayPal and at some point I was  at Facebook but what it's really done is  it's it's allowed me to think very  creatively about the problem solving  there are people who are making spheres  tsunami balls in Japan that are very  cost effective that didn't exist when I  started the project but this is I think  this is more like an art project than a  business

